; SET-MAR and CLEAR-MAR over a range of words (sys/sys/qmisc.lisp; contract
; G3 revision 14, 10.10): each page from the range's first word's to its last
; word's is visited once, the addresses ordered unsigned (SI::MAP-MAR-PAGES).
; The old loops stepped #o200 words and compared signed: past 2^31 they ended
; at once (rev14-addresses tests that), and on any machine they could miss
; the page holding the last word when it lay in that page's first 127 words,
; by LOW modulo 128.  Here the range runs from 28 words below a page boundary
; to 50 words past it, so the old loop visited only the first page, and a
; write of the last word did not trap while the page was in core.  Run with
;   --compile --files sys/sys2/lmmac.lisp,sys/sys/qmisc.lisp,tools/system-check/lisp/mar-range.lisp
; on any band.  The first two cases and the last are controls: a write of the
; first word traps, a write outside the range does not, and none once the MAR
; is cleared.  System 2001 without the change fails the third (measured).
(progn (mar-set 100. 20.) (mar-trap-p 100.)) => T
(prog1 (mar-trap-p 130.) (si:clear-mar)) => NIL
(let ((low (- (mar-index (mar-page-after 100.)) 28.))) (mar-set low 79.) (prog1 (mar-trap-p (+ low 78.)) (si:clear-mar))) => T
(let ((low (- (mar-index (mar-page-after 100.)) 28.))) (mar-set low 79.) (si:clear-mar) (or (mar-trap-p low) (mar-trap-p (+ low 78.)))) => NIL
